{"items":[{"owner":{"account_id":1566961,"reputation":1542,"user_id":62049,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":62,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/d0c9495c2b4db2649eec2b9ca8d956c9?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"TtT23","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/62049/ttt23"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1353298679,"post_id":1099,"comment_id":336449,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","body":"I found this book to be one of the most challenging books to read, but nonetheless a fantastic one."},{"owner":{"account_id":64194,"reputation":6152,"user_id":31290,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7e723155322cac970975d7223b55f27b?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"mcottle","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/31290/mcottle"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1310949983,"post_id":1595,"comment_id":169515,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","body":"Don&#39;t waste time reading this book.  Skim it or find a summary it&#39;s horribly bloated &amp; repeats the same (self evident) point several times in slightly different ways.  Probably ideal for teaching time management to the hard-of-thinking"},{"owner":{"account_id":36992,"reputation":1334,"user_id":170,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/c0a5a408364e67770fc1b5ae33b3384b?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"FeatureCreep","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/170/featurecreep"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1309516693,"post_id":1597,"comment_id":160479,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","body":"Here is a good complement to the book: <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Qo7vUdKTlhk\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">youtube.com/watch?v=Qo7vUdKTlhk</a>"},{"owner":{"account_id":84347,"reputation":101,"user_id":13118,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/257fff8f9ba57efabd93b3c94f4a4ab4?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Aaron S","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/13118/aaron-s"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1294905455,"post_id":1593,"comment_id":63232,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Same as Walter..."},{"owner":{"account_id":170074,"reputation":2976,"user_id":12854,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/cbcfa45e0170031552a9328c7b4dbe7e?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Sjoerd","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/12854/sjoerd"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1294700905,"post_id":5261,"comment_id":61635,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Lots of jokes in ICT refer to this book, especially jokes found in old source code."},{"owner":{"account_id":20180,"reputation":856,"user_id":8769,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/d3149cf105b708746f1c4eb0a63a5c24?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"j_random_hacker","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/8769/j-random-hacker"},"edited":false,"score":10,"creation_date":1294383048,"post_id":1593,"comment_id":59527,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"It&#39;s funny that this appears right after &quot;How to Win Friends and Influence People&quot;...  &quot;If plan A fails, there&#39;s always plan B...&quot;  :)"},{"owner":{"account_id":13147,"reputation":8560,"user_id":148,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/UNGHL.png?s=256","display_name":"Paul Nathan","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/148/paul-nathan"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1294351613,"post_id":2849,"comment_id":59435,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I&#39;ve been very impressed by Alexander and Gabriel&#39;s writings on patterns and software, and, dually, disappointed by the &quot;Object Oriented Design Patterns&quot; movement."},{"owner":{"account_id":30551,"reputation":1163,"user_id":11206,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/92a1203dd766cfafabdfa21c3b196454?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"mctylr","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/11206/mctylr"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":42964,"reputation":1073,"user_id":1454,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ad5a692e6c564556953c2db8a51bdab2?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"MAK","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1454/mak"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1294348813,"post_id":1724,"comment_id":59415,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"@MAK, they are actually more about software management than about actual programming directly. They are classics that I strongly recommend to any if not every professional developer for becoming a more well rounded developer. I admit they are at the fuzzy <i>border</i> of whether they are programming or non-programming books about development/software management."},{"owner":{"account_id":43037,"reputation":2245,"user_id":4982,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5dcf9c84cdc5d8e39116b880187afbbd?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Huperniketes","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/4982/huperniketes"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1294335624,"post_id":11893,"comment_id":59317,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Actually, two of the book&#39;s authors, Max Jacobson and Murray Silverstein, worked with Christopher Alexander (and others) to assemble those patterns.  But again, while APL focused on the patterns to be implemented in a residential structure, this book focuses on patterns for designing/judging a well-designed home. It gives remarkable insight into determining how to design a software system well, or if it was designed so."},{"owner":{"account_id":65147,"reputation":11104,"user_id":12354,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7baab1a930992c97d5b8efd48071ace8?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Homde","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/12354/homde"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1294328859,"post_id":1595,"comment_id":59210,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Although being a bit to &quot;self-improvish&quot;, The &quot;Sharpening the saw&quot; principle is about the most important things you can learn as a programmer"},{"owner":{"account_id":65147,"reputation":11104,"user_id":12354,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7baab1a930992c97d5b8efd48071ace8?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Homde","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/12354/homde"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1294328688,"post_id":11893,"comment_id":59206,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Maybe it&#39;s not surprising, the book is probably inspired by the seminal work of Christopher Alexander  &quot;A Pattern language&quot;, the guy who <b>invented</b> design patterns for use in architecture, the concept was later adopted by computerscience and the gang of four"},{"owner":{"account_id":26625,"reputation":11393,"user_id":4854,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/02e56b30e8b319fd2e29b13a778a3f7f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"TMN","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/4854/tmn"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1291647175,"post_id":2919,"comment_id":38771,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Yep.  I have a quote from this book posted right above my monitor."},{"owner":{"user_type":"does_not_exist","display_name":"user1539"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1291645324,"post_id":1099,"comment_id":38746,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I know a lot of people speak highly of this book - but I found it extremely difficult to follow."},{"owner":{"account_id":69161,"reputation":282,"user_id":3057,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/907b337cfd1d8d8e71203c57263b9819?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Srinivas Reddy Thatiparthy","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/3057/srinivas-reddy-thatiparthy"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1291641617,"post_id":1595,"comment_id":38718,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"-1 these kind of books put more pressure on us."},{"owner":{"account_id":32276,"reputation":22764,"user_id":5095,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/67f14999bf99b9826c79fa7d2be58db6?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Jon Hopkins","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/5095/jon-hopkins"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1290167784,"post_id":1595,"comment_id":30341,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I detested the 7HoHEP.  A friend once commented that the first habit of highly effective people was not wasting time reading books like this.  I get that others disagree but I found this about 50 pages of interesting (though sometimes obvious) material bulked up to justify a book."},{"owner":{"account_id":26816,"reputation":1962,"user_id":3755,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/28a8b24aab4348fb5408085c24b9ff88?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Amit Wadhwa","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/3755/amit-wadhwa"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1288411245,"post_id":1597,"comment_id":22977,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I agree with Yan here, I personally think a lot of the chapters can be skimmed over and some need to read in detail."},{"owner":{"account_id":71093,"reputation":16146,"user_id":101,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/09941fead3a8de71294d0e5a4e0a84eb?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Walter","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/101/walter"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1288398554,"post_id":1593,"comment_id":22948,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I wish I could vote more than once for this."},{"owner":{"account_id":9520,"reputation":22009,"user_id":5512,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/0bce4ecc3649443edeb6eba28f9a6c04?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Scott Whitlock","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/5512/scott-whitlock"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1288398049,"post_id":2919,"comment_id":22947,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"This is a great book, and the follow up, &quot;Lila&quot; is just as good.  He sets out to create a new &quot;metaphysics&quot;, and I think he failed to do that, but by the end of the book he <i>succeeds</i> at specifying an algorithm that codifies western values: given any two things, you can use his &quot;metaphysics of quality&quot; to figure out which one western society values more.  I think that&#39;s quite the accomplishment, though I&#39;m not sure that&#39;s how he sees it."},{"owner":{"account_id":102233,"reputation":262,"user_id":1524,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/qo37a.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Yan Sklyarenko","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1524/yan-sklyarenko"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1288075874,"post_id":1597,"comment_id":21050,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"As for me, it could be much thiner. The same concepts are explained in this book over and over, which doesn&#39;t adds more value. But that&#39;s IMHO :)"},{"owner":{"account_id":43037,"reputation":2245,"user_id":4982,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5dcf9c84cdc5d8e39116b880187afbbd?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Huperniketes","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/4982/huperniketes"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1287027822,"post_id":1016,"comment_id":16542,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"The expanded edition is the &quot;director&#39;s cut&quot; printed in 2-colors black + red) and with an added appendix (10 1/2 Commandments of Visual Thinking, which is a nice recap of things to keep in mind). There might be additional content, but I don&#39;t have the first edition so I can&#39;t contrast them."},{"owner":{"account_id":3774,"reputation":3724,"user_id":3963,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/750159e9cdab58c4b6547d382311c9af?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Kyralessa","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/3963/kyralessa"},"edited":false,"score":8,"creation_date":1287024892,"post_id":10817,"comment_id":16534,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"This is a book whose title gives entirely the wrong impression.  It sounds like it&#39;s about how to manipulate people.  In fact, it&#39;s about how to get along with people and inspire people by being a good, decent person."},{"owner":{"user_type":"does_not_exist","display_name":"user1249"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1287009735,"post_id":5261,"comment_id":16451,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"But quite silly :)  I love it though.."},{"owner":{"user_type":"does_not_exist","display_name":"user1249"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1287009462,"post_id":1099,"comment_id":16449,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Hear, hear, fantastic book!"},{"owner":{"account_id":77792,"reputation":10816,"user_id":389,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/23y8L.png?s=256","display_name":"AArteDoCodigo.com.br - Maniero","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/389/aartedocodigo-com-br-maniero"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":86603,"reputation":2138,"user_id":4906,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":83,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/Fwvne.png?s=256","display_name":"stakx","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/4906/stakx"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1286741525,"post_id":2919,"comment_id":14903,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"@stakx: Exactly. Did you read the question? None books here is about software. It&#39;s good reading to help us to write better software. If a reader can&#39;t understand how it applies to software development..."},{"owner":{"account_id":35990,"reputation":6779,"user_id":572,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/etoxY.gif?s=256","display_name":"JBRWilkinson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/572/jbrwilkinson"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1286738678,"post_id":10817,"comment_id":14883,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Although the example scenarios are a little old now, the practical aspects of this book still hold today."},{"owner":{"account_id":35990,"reputation":6779,"user_id":572,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/etoxY.gif?s=256","display_name":"JBRWilkinson","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/572/jbrwilkinson"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1286738605,"post_id":5261,"comment_id":14882,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I have to say that the BBC Radiophonic Workshop version of Hitchhikers is <b>absolutely awesome</b> - lots of amazing sound effects, so you are completely engrossed and feel like you are there with Ford, Zaphod, Arthur and Trillian, et al."},{"owner":{"account_id":86603,"reputation":2138,"user_id":4906,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":83,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/Fwvne.png?s=256","display_name":"stakx","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/4906/stakx"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1286715578,"post_id":2919,"comment_id":14802,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"<i>&quot;It teach us how to do right maintenance on software.&quot;</i> -- It&#39;s an interesting book, but it certainly didn&#39;t teach <i>me</i> anything about software. It&#39;s more like an introduction to philosophy."},{"owner":{"account_id":70446,"reputation":393,"user_id":1209,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/97c1d7c7d7d48017ce55936bff356688?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"HerbN","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1209/herbn"},"edited":false,"score":13,"creation_date":1285480544,"post_id":2997,"comment_id":8908,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"This are both programming books."},{"owner":{"account_id":77792,"reputation":10816,"user_id":389,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/23y8L.png?s=256","display_name":"AArteDoCodigo.com.br - Maniero","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/389/aartedocodigo-com-br-maniero"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1284918146,"post_id":1597,"comment_id":5675,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"It&#39;s funny. You need read the entire book to learn how to finish the book :-)"},{"owner":{"account_id":42964,"reputation":1073,"user_id":1454,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/ad5a692e6c564556953c2db8a51bdab2?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"MAK","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1454/mak"},"edited":false,"score":4,"creation_date":1284916725,"post_id":1724,"comment_id":5664,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"They are still all programming books. A programming book is not necessarily always about a specific language/technology."},{"owner":{"account_id":10833,"reputation":223,"user_id":1663,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/28d0e5f930c06474b38ee290c8fe644c?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"blizpasta","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/1663/blizpasta"},"edited":false,"score":9,"creation_date":1284903099,"post_id":1597,"comment_id":5611,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Sadly, I got this book 5-6 years ago and my bookmark is still somewhere in the middle of it."},{"owner":{"account_id":6190,"reputation":289,"user_id":422,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/bc5f7b22cb566874c685508a7bfc2af2?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"logoin","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/422/logoin"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1284496572,"post_id":1595,"comment_id":3529,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"I&#39;m reading this book and find it helpful in determining my priority in life."},{"owner":{"account_id":36992,"reputation":1334,"user_id":170,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/c0a5a408364e67770fc1b5ae33b3384b?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"FeatureCreep","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/170/featurecreep"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1284137244,"post_id":985,"comment_id":2250,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Added to my reading list."},{"owner":{"account_id":49912,"reputation":6173,"user_id":61,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/07d542a58ef9867b4ac2309ecdac3d2e?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Chinmay Kanchi","link":"https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/users/61/chinmay-kanchi"},"edited":false,"score":10,"creation_date":1283691071,"post_id":982,"comment_id":801,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 2.5","body":"Heh, I wouldn&#39;t be too keen on reading a book on design that had a cover with that colourscheme ;)"}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":254}